From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:43:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: fix a leak in VrrUnstallTimer

A fired timer stays allocated until nvkms_free_timer() is called on its handle.
VrrUnstallTimer() cleared the handle without freeing it, so every timer that
fired leaked its nvkms_timer_t. Only timers that were canceled before firing
were freed. Free it from the callback, like IdleTimerProc() does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-vrr.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-vrr.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-vrr.c
index d8167a28..d6c6d1b6 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-vrr.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-vrr.c
@@ -958,6 +958,7 @@ VrrUnstallTimer(void *dataPtr, NvU32 dataU32)
     NVDispEvoPtr pDispEvo = dataPtr;
 
     VrrUnstallNow(pDispEvo);
+    nvkms_free_timer(pDispEvo->vrr.unstallTimer);
     pDispEvo->vrr.unstallTimer = NULL;
 }
 
